# Template switch remaps SQL backups

Full log: [docs/AUDIT.md](docs/AUDIT.md) (2026-09-14, leftover discovered SQL hostname).

After adopt, the live DB is `{slug}_postgres` or `{slug}_mysql` (`{slug}-db`). Old discovered names (`legacy-postgres-2`, `{slug}-postgres`) must not keep dump jobs.

- `upsert_database_config` replaces stale connections and remaps backup `connection_id`s.
- Discovery must skip `managed` apps so repo compose hostnames are not re-added.
- Dump fallback uses the panel host only when the stored container is gone.
- Do **not** recreate the old discovered SQL container. Do **not** dump via generic hostname `postgres` from `vps_dashboard`.

File backups are path syncs; they do not need this remap. SQLite addons have no `{slug}-db`.

App-file dest is the selected remote folder. Sync **contents** of the chosen path (`storage/app/public/attachments`), not `dest/storage/app/...`. Do not pre-check whole `storage/app`. See [docs/AUDIT.md](docs/AUDIT.md) (2026-09-15, app files dump). **Always append AUDIT.md** when you change backup jobs.